## 1. Windows Network Troubleshooting

When a user reports that they cannot access the Internet or a network resource, I should investigate the issue systematically instead of immediately changing network settings.

### Initial Questions

- When did the issue start?
- Is the issue affecting only one user or multiple users?
- Can the user access other websites or network resources?
- Are other devices experiencing the same problem?
- Were any recent changes made to the computer or network?

### Troubleshooting Workflow

```text
Gather Information
        ↓
Determine the Scope
        ↓
Check Network Configuration
        ↓
Test Local and External Connectivity
        ↓
Investigate DNS or DHCP
        ↓
Apply an Authorized Fix
        ↓
Retest and Verify
        ↓
Document the Resolution
```

