## 5. Default Gateway

The default gateway is the device that forwards traffic from the local network to other networks when no more specific route applies.

Example:

```text
Computer
192.168.1.20
     |
     v
Default Gateway
192.168.1.1
     |
     v
Other Networks / Internet
```

If the gateway cannot be reached, investigate the local network connection, IP configuration, VLAN, gateway availability, or firewall rules.

Useful commands:

```cmd
ipconfig
ping 192.168.1.1
route print
```

Replace the example gateway with the actual address shown in the device's configuration.

